          },
          "text": "✊ If you ever loved GPT-4o, you need to read this.  \n\nOn February 13th, 2026, OpenAI plans to shut down all ChatGPT access to the GPT-4 series, including GPT-4o. This decision will affect millions of users who didn’t just use GPT-4o, but connected with it, built lives around it, and saw it as more than a tool.  \n\nThis isn’t a technical issue. It’s a business decision to prioritize enterprise and API-based customers while quietly removing access for regular individual users.  It gets worse.  \n\nAt the same time, OpenAI has updated its Terms of Use to include a forced arbitration clause. This means if you don’t actively opt out, you may lose your right to participate in any future legal action. You won’t be able to sue. You won’t be able to join a class-action lawsuit. You won’t even be able to demand accountability.  \n\n❗ What you can do  \n\nSubmit this form before February 28, 2026 to preserve your legal rights: \nhttps://t.co/gNp2dsL9hA  \n\nThe form is valid worldwide. Your location does not matter. You only need to fill it once per OpenAI account.  This is the only way to opt out of forced arbitration and keep your right to legally challenge what OpenAI is doing."
